  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 2055.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pp3ppp/2n1bn2/2p5/2P5/5N2/PP1P1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 7",
   "line": [
    "Nc6"
   ],
   "spoken": "With the knight to c6 Black grips the key central squares, making it genuinely hard for White to untangle and develop. The initiative, not the pawn count, defines the position.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "When down a pawn for activity, clamp the squares that keep the opponent tangled.",
   "plans": "Keep the pieces active and the white king stuck in the centre."
